cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the
  paper it formalizes. S. Armstrong was supported by NSF grant DMS-2350340 and
  by the European Research Council (ERC) under the European Union's Horizon
  Europe research and innovation programme, grant agreement number 101200828.
  V. Vicol was supported by the Collaborative NSF grant DMS-2307681 and by a
  Simons Investigator Award.
title: "AVAnomalousRegularization: a Lean 4 formalization of anomalous regularization of passive scalars up to the Obukhov–Corrsin exponent"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-04
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of S. Armstrong and V.
  Vicol, "Anomalous regularization of passive scalars up to the
  Obukhov–Corrsin exponent". For the advection-diffusion equation on the
  two-dimensional torus with a divergence-free, alpha-Hölder velocity field
  constructed as in Armstrong and Vicol, "Anomalous diffusion by fractal
  homogenization", alpha < 1/3, it proves that, for every s below the
  Obukhov–Corrsin exponent (1 - alpha)/2 and with the velocity field depending
  on s, at positive times the solutions are bounded in C^{0,s} by a constant
  times the L^2 norm of the initial datum, uniformly in the diffusivity in a
  union of bands accumulating at zero (Theorem A); that every
  solution dissipates a fixed fraction of its variance in unit time, with
  constants independent of the diffusivity, the L^2 datum and the initial time
  (Theorem B); a local form of Theorem A in space-time tubes that follow the
  flow of a coarse velocity field (Theorem C); and the vanishing-diffusivity limits (Corollary D). The
  proofs use only the standard axioms.
